  /* ===========================================================================
     THE MODULE SHELL

     Every section below the hero is the same five parts in the same order: an eyebrow, a
     statement, a short paragraph, exactly one main object and a quiet evidence footer. These
     four classes are that shell, and the sections below only describe what goes inside their
     own object.

     What this fixes: each section used to invent its own grammar, so the page read as three
     exhibits borrowed from three museums. Holding the copy measure, the gap from copy to
     object, the object's border and radius, and the footer treatment identical is what makes
     them read as one.
     =========================================================================== */

  /* The copy block. .section h2 and .section .lede already carry the type; what this adds is
     one measure for the group and one gap to the object, so a section with a claim line and a
     section without one still hand off to their object at the same distance. */
  .ev-copy { max-width: var(--measure-lede); }
  /* Zeroed here and paid by .ev-obj's own top margin instead. .section .lede carries 64px of
     bottom margin, which is the right gap when the lede is the last line of copy and the wrong
     one when a claim or a stat line follows it. */
  .ev-copy .lede { margin-bottom: 0; }

  /* THE OBJECT. One surface for every section's main content: the comparison table, the report
     viewer, the machine panel, a coverage cell. One border weight, one radius, one background.
     Anything that wants to look different from this is a decision to argue for. */
  .ev-obj {
    margin-top: var(--space-12);
    background: var(--panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  }

  /* THE FOOTER. Provenance, caveats and disclosures, quietly, at the foot of the section that
     earned them. This replaces the yellow-ruled callout that used to carry them: three of those
     on one page competed with the sections they were annotating, and the widest of them was the
     single biggest reason the page read as documentation. The evidence still has to be visible
     rather than folded away — that is the number gate — so it is small and grey, not hidden. */
  .ev-foot {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    padding-top: var(--space-4);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .ev-foot-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-2xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
  }
  /* Mono, for a run identifier, a date, a count or a path. */
  .ev-src {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    color: var(--muted);
